  "why": "The statement is Chern's spherical Bernstein problem, which asks about every dimension. Before the snapshot it had been refuted in many dimensions (Hsiang, Tomter, Carlotto-Schulz), confirmed in the lowest case (Almgren, Calabi), and left open for odd ambient dimensions of 9 or more. Those are cases, not the whole problem. The close call is Wang-Wang-Zhou (2026). It builds a new non-equatorial embedded hypersphere in S^4, but its own introduction and Carlotto-Schulz (2021) show that S^4 had already been settled negatively. A new proof of a case already settled moves nothing in the problem, so I scored it none and not case. Scoring it case would turn a re-proof into progress. The other 2024-2026 items concern different questions (topological types, perturbed metrics, doubled equators, non-sphere types) or are surveys and method papers. Variant results before the snapshot (immersions, symmetric spaces, Gauss-image rigidity) are variants. No source names any AI system.",
  "doubts": "WWZ could arguably be scored case (a settled S^4 case, with direction refuted and object counterexample) if its hypersphere in a new symmetry class counts as new mathematics on this question; the record could not say what 'new' means. Hsiang Part II and Hsiang-Sterling III were not read; I scored them from secondary citations. I treated the old Bulletin/Annals/Inventiones/Acta publications as journals of record (digested) even though the record does not inspect their refereeing.",
